# workflows authoring

**Read [`memory/workflows-authoring.md`](../memory/workflows-authoring.md) before going further.** This rule exists to
fire on the topic and send you there; the knowledge itself lives in one place, not two.

**Why it is worth the read:** The workflow runtime forbids more than it looks like it does -- no filesystem, no require, no Date.now -- and `parallel()` reports total failure and a genuinely empty result identically.

## Before you touch anything

- A `null` from `parallel()` means that branch FAILED, not that it found nothing. Return an explicit failure when every branch is null; three dead agents once reported a clean "no candidates surfaced".
- Scripts have no filesystem and no `require`. Anything a script needs must be inline or arrive through `args`.
- Phases cost six figures of tokens each. They are once-per-feature commands, not casual ones.

